{
  "name": "tank_hall",
  "version": 1,
  "introduced_by": "gannet",
  "notes": "Ruined seawater tank hall, 14 m by 22 m and 9 m to the ridge, concrete walls with clerestory windows and corrugated sheet over steel trusses, the rear half of the roof gone; eight holding tanks in two rows either side of a wide aisle, two cracked, some full of rainwater and weed. The front door (local -Z) is an empty doorway. It carves nothing.",
